    <!-- 4. AI RISK FORMULA TAB -->
    <div id="tab-airisk" class="hidden-tab">
      <div style="background:#0f172a; color:#fff; border-radius:18px; padding:28px; margin-bottom:24px;">
        <h3 style="font-size:20px; font-weight:800; color:#fbbf24; margin-bottom:8px;">The Mathematical Composite Formula</h3>
        <p style="color:#cbd5e1; font-size:14px; line-height:1.6; margin-bottom:16px;">
          Automation probability is not a simplistic binary score. We decompose each degree's primary job paths into atomic tasks, evaluate task substitutability across 7 research frameworks, and adjust for Sri Lankan economic conditions:
        </p>
        <div style="background:rgba(255,255,255,0.08); padding:16px; border-radius:12px; font-family:'Courier New', monospace; font-size:16px; color:#f8fafc;">
          R<sub>degree</sub> = Σ<sub>i=1..7</sub> (w<sub>i</sub> · F<sub>i</sub> · T<sub>i</sub>) + α · C<sub>SL</sub> − β · H<sub>human</sub>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="pillar-card">
        <h4 style="font-size:16px; font-weight:800; color:#0f172a; margin-bottom:8px;">Framework Breakdown:</h4>
        <ul style="padding-left:20px; font-size:14px; color:#475569; line-height:1.7;">
          <li><strong>Framework 01:</strong> Task-probability Computerisation Model (Frey &amp; Osborne)</li>
          <li><strong>Framework 02:</strong> Task-based Substitution Mechanics (Acemoglu &amp; Restrepo)</li>
          <li><strong>Framework 03:</strong> Global Workforce &amp; Job Creation Outlook (WEF Future of Jobs)</li>
          <li><strong>Framework 04:</strong> Skill-Demand Velocity Shift Index</li>
          <li><strong>Framework 05:</strong> Cognitive vs Routine Axis Decomposition</li>
          <li><strong>Framework 06:</strong> Large Language Model (LLM) Direct Exposure Index (OpenAI &amp; Eloundou)</li>
          <li><strong>Framework 07:</strong> Sri Lankan Labour-Market Model &amp; Public Sector Absorption (C<sub>SL</sub>)</li>
          <li><strong>Protective Shield (H<sub>human</sub>):</strong> Human empathy, physical dexterity, medical judgment, and legal responsibility factor.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

